==English==

===Etymology===
Prefix "neo-" (from greek 'neos'= "new") and "tropical" (from greek 'tropikos', referring to where the length of the day equals that of the night)

===Noun===
{{en-plural-noun}}

# [[tropical|Tropical]] [[America]]: the tropical areas of [[North America|North]], [[Central America|Central]] and [[South America]]. The [[tropics]] of "the new world". Used in biology (Not to be confused with the [[wikipedia:Neotropic|Neotropic (singular) or Neotropical ecozone]] as used by Schultz, something else entirely).

